ng is testimony  and witness about joe biden  which she did in talking about what she  knows in the personal joe biden  that's what they're trying to do all  week and she did all three of those  things  yeah it seems that even the republicans  were saying that michelle obama  knocked it out of the park last night  but what do you make of this virtual  convention  do you think it delivered i think it's  so hard to have these kind of  events with no audience when you're so  propelled by the audience applause  you know when we talk about this people  think why are we so obsessed with the  way it looks and the theatrics of this  well because what conventions do at  least in the modern age is use the  theatrics  as a kind of freight train on which they  put the message and that's to energize  the the base it's also to speak to  undecided voters and also try to put the  opposition in a box  so how it comes across matters and i  think that there are obviously they were  wrestling with that what we will see is  whether a speech like michelle obama's  which was clearly the highlight of the  night gets passed around in social media  and on youtube and the rest of it and if  that's the case then it does what a  traditional convention tries to do  there are all kinds of internal things  they're trying to do too you know  bernie sanders speech was a message of  unity for his supporters kind of narrow  casting there  handing the microphone over to regular  people was a nice touch in terms of  trying to  speak to that unity message so there  were some some  nice attempts to do what you would  normally do in a convention  but i think the real question is how  does it live on  afterwards in the social media world  to see if it really has any effect  that's long lasting  in past conventions it seems that they  would highlight rising stars  in this particular convention when you  look up the lineup they're going back to  a lot of the  i don't want to say older leaders but  past leader